  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 226 PM MDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nThe center of the retrograding upper-low will center itself over far \nnorthern NM on Friday, keeping upslope flow in place over the \nSacramento Mountains. There will also likely be a low cloud deck \nacross the eastern plains, which will keep high temps down, with \nhighs running 10 to 15 degrees below average. The pleasant Fall \nweather will continue into the weekend as temperatures slowly \nmoderate close to seasonal averages. Dry weather with mostly clear \nto partly cloudy skies will continue through the weekend. Ridging \nwill amplify over the Intermountain West early next week, keeping \nthe warming trend going.\n\nZonal to northwest flow will attempt to squash this ridge Tuesday. \nGiven the very positive tilt of the trough, it would likely \nstruggle to draw significant sub-tropical moisture northward. \nNeither ensemble system is bullish on widespread rainfall, with all \nshowing less than 0.25\" areawide. Amplified ridging will likely \npersist over the western CONUS through the end of next week, \nfavoring dry weather and near to slightly above average\ntemperatures.",
